From a03f4803016215f9109f94b9dc213723a0333025 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sneid1 <sneid1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:42:45 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] UYA textures: PCSX2 names, dumps, replacements and coverage
 on the GS-full pipe

The GS front end keeps its own copy of local memory (uploads and local copies in GIF order) and names every texture a prim
samples the way PCSX2 does (texpack::gsname), without waiting for the rasteriser. Drawn-into blocks are tracked per byte plane
(low 24 bits, top byte) and per prim's page rows, since UYA keeps T8H / T4HL / T4HH textures in the top byte of its CT24 display
and Z24 depth buffers and streams textures into the rows a frame does not draw. Per name: a dump as <name>.png (texpack::live::
Dumper), the replacement from a PCSX2 folder (texpack::live::Live: decoded, validated, mip chain), sampled by the software GS in
place of the original (gs_raster::sample_repl), and a texture id written with every pixel into a coverage plane that follows
blits, T8 read-backs and local copies (Gs::cover_ids).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
